# Structural correctness (do not regress these)

- ES/NQ `sw1` and `sw2` swing comparisons must use **EXACT** timestamp match —
  zero tolerance, same bar only. Never loosen this to a ±N minute tolerance,
  even to raise signal count. (This is defect **S3** — see the v8.8 audit-scope
  rule for its audit ID and current fix status.)
- FVG search must start from `sw2_conf_idx`, not from the signal bar.

## Entry-type timing — two protocols, do not mix them

`SMT_IN_FVG` and `FVG_AFTER_SMT` have **separate** timing protocols. Do not
apply SMT_IN_FVG's confirmation-bar rule to FVG_AFTER_SMT, and do not treat
a failed SMT_IN_FVG confirmation as an automatic FVG_AFTER_SMT.

### SMT_IN_FVG — confirmation is exactly 1 minute after sw2

- Confirmation must occur **exactly 1 minute after `sw2_conf_time`** (the
  very next real bar). Verify by **elapsed timestamp**, not by a positional
  `sw2_conf_idx + 1` with a gap ceiling.
- Any elapsed gap other than exactly 1 minute means the swing's true next
  bar does not exist in `sdf` (a session boundary). Reject the SMT_IN_FVG
  candidate **outright**.
- Do **not** fall back to FVG_AFTER_SMT automatically.
- Do **not** loosely accept up to `MAX_CONF_GAP_MINS` (currently 5).
- Pre-existing FVG membership, `entry_price`, and `smt_time` all reference
  that same confirmation bar (`sw2_conf_time + 1 minute`), not the outer-loop
  scan bar `i`. Cached candidates can be re-emitted many bars later; stamping
  `row['et']` would attach a later, unrelated bar.

### FVG_AFTER_SMT — entry is whenever a valid post-SMT FVG forms

- Entry occurs whenever `find_fvg()`'s pattern search locates a valid
  post-SMT FVG. That can be several bars after sw2, gated by
  `FVG_LOOKAHEAD` — **not** fixed to sw2 + 1 minute.
- FVG_AFTER_SMT is constrained only by its own FVG-formation timing
  (lookahead, 3-bar contiguity, in-session FVG). It is **not** constrained
  by SMT_IN_FVG's confirmation-bar / `MAX_CONF_GAP_MINS` rule.
- `smt_time` for FVG_AFTER_SMT is the FVG-formation bar timestamp, not
  `sw2_conf_idx + 1` and not scan bar `i`.

**Known code bug (flagged, not fixed in this documentation pass):**
`confirmation_bar_is_contiguous()` / `MAX_CONF_GAP_MINS` currently runs on
every candidate **before** the `if pre_fvg:` SMT_IN_FVG vs FVG_AFTER_SMT
branch. That can wrongly reject a valid FVG_AFTER_SMT whose protocol never
depended on sw2+1 contiguity. A later code pass must apply the exact-1-minute
confirmation check **only** on the SMT_IN_FVG path.

## Session windows — one canonical definition

`SESSIONS` = NY Morning 08:00–10:30, NY Afternoon 13:00–15:00.
`SESSION_CUTOFF_MINS = 30`. `sdf` is built from `classify_bar()` results
that are not `None` (session + pre_session), then `reset_index`, so
consecutive `sdf` indices are **not** always consecutive minutes.

A bar is **"in session"** only if it survives the same cutoff used to
classify session bars when building `sdf`:

- session: `ss <= t < se - SESSION_CUTOFF_MINS`
  (NY Morning 08:00–10:00, NY Afternoon 13:00–14:30)
- pre_session (in `sdf` for swing context, **not** "in session"):
  `ss - PRE_SESSION_LOOKBACK_MINS <= t < ss`
- everything else, including the 30 minutes before each session end
  (10:00–10:30, 14:30–15:00), is out of session and must not be treated
  as an in-session bar

`classify_bar()` and `fvg_in_session()` **must both use this cutoff**.
There must not be two different definitions of "in session" in the same
file.

**Known mismatch (flagged, not fixed in this pass):** `fvg_in_session()`
currently uses the raw `SESSIONS` end times (08:00–10:30 / 13:00–15:00)
with no cutoff, so 10:00–10:30 and 14:30–15:00 count as in-session for
FVGs while `classify_bar()` / `sdf` session bars exclude them.

## FVG 3-bar window

- A 3-bar FVG (`j-1`, `j`, `j+1`) must be consecutive 1-minute bars.
  `fvg_in_session()` on the middle bar is not enough; `find_fvg` must
  reject any window whose elapsed time is not 1+1 minutes. Piece 3 must
  fail any FVG_AFTER_SMT whose `fvg_bar` spans a session gap
  (`check_fvg_windows_contiguous`).

## FVG_AFTER_SMT stop-loss

- SL anchors to the most recent swing low (LONG) or swing high (SHORT)
  whose **timestamp is strictly before the FVG bar's timestamp**.
- Do **not** compare a positional `sdf` index against a swing-history
  snapshot taken at whatever bar the candidate was last evaluated on
  (the outer-loop scan bar `i`).
- Re-derive the lookup **fresh at the FVG bar**, not by reusing an
  earlier scan-bar snapshot.

**Known mismatch (flagged, not fixed in this pass):** SL currently walks
`sl_*_hist` / `sh_*_hist` from scan bar `i` and keeps the last swing with
`s[1] < fvg_bar_idx` (positional).

## Macro bias / 5m confluence clock

- `combined_15m_bias` and `smt5m_status` must be evaluated as of the
  **confirmation bar's timestamp**, not the outer scan loop's current bar
  `i`. Same principle as the `smt_time` scan-bar bug, extended to these
  two fields, and respecting the SMT_IN_FVG vs FVG_AFTER_SMT timing
  distinction above:
  - SMT_IN_FVG: `sw2_conf_time + 1 minute`
  - FVG_AFTER_SMT: the FVG-formation bar
- Cached candidates re-evaluated many bars later must not pick up a later
  15m bucket or 5m confluence state.

**Known mismatch (flagged, not fixed in this pass):** both fields are
currently keyed off `row['et']` (scan `i`) and cached on that bar's
15m/5m floor.

## Dedup

- Dedup on exact `(date, sw2_conf_time, direction, instrument)` identity.
  Prefer SMT_IN_FVG over FVG_AFTER_SMT when both exist for the same sw2
  (`keep='first'` after ranking).
- **Not** a 30-minute `smt_time` bucket. v8.7 abandoned the bucket because
  the same SMT (identical sw1/sw2) could spawn a new signal each time
  `smt_time` crossed a 30-min boundary; identity on `sw2_conf_time` fires
  each unique SMT once.

## Wick SMT / equal high-low

- SMT divergence must be measured on **wicks**, at structural
  swing-marker-tagged points only — never candle bodies or non-structural
  points. (Audit-confirmed as the primary driver of false signals and losses.)
- Equal-high/equal-low SMT requires exact price match (`EQUAL_THRESHOLD = 0.0`)
  — never a tolerance band.
